2026-10-26T03:07:00Z  CHANGE   src/qml/components/KaraokeMaster.qml: the three "animated dots" set `opacity: 0.3 + 0.7*Math.abs(Math.sin(Date.now()/500 + index))` inside a binding. `Date.now()` is not a bindable property, so the expression is evaluated once at delegate creation and the dots never move. Replaced with a looping SequentialAnimation on opacity (PauseAnimation index*140 ms, then 420 ms up and 420 ms down, InOutSine).
2026-10-26T03:07:00Z  CHANGE   src/qml/components/VisualizerOverlay.qml: the glow backdrop's `scale: 1.0 + (isPlaying ? 0.05*Math.sin(Date.now()/100) : 0)` had the same defect, plus it bound to `AudioBridge.isPlaying` so the frozen value was whichever state existed at creation. Now a SequentialAnimation on scale gated on the overlay's own `glow` flag and `AudioBridge.isPlaying`. The delegate's other `modelData.*` uses were also given defaults (posX/posY/baseOpacity/textColor/glowing/animation, and text/fontSize/bold in the Text) because these values come from JSON-persisted overlay state: `undefined * width` is NaN, which QML turns into an invisible item at a nonsense position instead of an error.
